  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammad Sabir Khalid Khan vs The State Of Maharashtra on 12 October, 2023 Author: N. J. Jamadar Bench: N. J. Jamadar 903-ABA2861-2023.ODT Santosh IN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT BOMBAY CRIMINAL APPELLATE JURISDICTION ANTICIPATORY BAIL APPLICATION NO. 2861 OF 2023 Mohammad Sabir Khalid Khan ...Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra ... CORAM: N. J. JAMADAR, J. 2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.289 of 2022, registered with Taloja Police Station, Navi Mumbai, for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 188, 272 and 273 read with Section 34 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 (\"the Penal Code\") and Sections 26, 27 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "facts": "2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.289 of 2022, registered with Taloja Police Station, Navi Mumbai, for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 188, 272 and 273 read with Section 34 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 (\"the Penal Code\") and Sections 26, 27 and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. The applicant has approached this Court under Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973, seeking pre-arrest bail. The apprehension of arrest is in connection with Crime Register No. 289 of 2023 registered with Taloja Police Station. The offences alleged are under Sections 328, 467, 468, 471, 292, 273, 188 read with Section 34 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860, and Sections 26(2)(i), 26, 27, and 51 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. Mohammad Sabir Khalid Khan vs The State Of Maharashtra on 29 September, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/44898829/ 1 2. The prosecution case, in short, is that on 28 October 2022, at about 5:30 a.m., PI Shinge and Kamble noticed a Ballero tempo bearing registration No. MH-04/JK-8429 coming from Mumbra side. The police party stopped the tempo near the toll plaza and 6-aba-2861-2023.doc carried out inspection. On checking, it was found to be carrying tobacco, pan masala, gutkha, and other such articles, collectively valued at Rs.10,15,780/-. The persons apprehended from the tempo disclosed that the said contraband was purchased from the present applicant. On this basis, the FIR came to be registered. 3. The learned Advocate appearing for the applicant submitted that this Court, by order dated 12 October 2023, granted interim protection to the applicant.",
    "arguments": "The applicant has not misused the liberty so granted and has cooperated in the investigation. The investigation is now complete and charge-sheet has been filed. Hence, it is prayed that the interim order of protection be made absolute. 4. On the other hand, the learned APP opposed the application. It was contended that the allegations against the applicant are serious in nature. Considering the gravity of the offence, the application ought to be rejected. It was further submitted that after the passing of the interim order, an additional charge under Section 467 of the Indian Penal Code has also been added by the prosecution.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The applicant has not misused the liberty so granted and has cooperated in the investigation. The investigation is now complete and charge-sheet has been filed. Hence, it is prayed that the interim order of protection be made absolute. 4. On the other hand, the learned APP opposed the application. It was contended that the allegations against the applicant are serious in nature.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Considering the gravity of the offence, the application ought to be rejected. It was further submitted that after the passing of the interim order, an additional charge under Section 467 of the Indian Penal Code has also been added by the prosecution.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
